ts turn limit. It ran out of turns after 40 turns, with 47 tests still failing. It had edited five of the six files and hadn't touched `sets.py`.\n\nI did not review the diff before bringing its branch in with `git merge --ff-only`. I read the diff afterwards, while finishing the work. Its changes are still uncommitted-on-top: the branch is merged, and my edits sit unstaged on top of it.\n\nI finished the rest myself:\n- **`sets.py`:** `PYTHONIOENCODING` is now exported together with the other exported variables, and `set_env_factory` accepts `SetEnvReference` and lists that contain references.\n- **`toml/_replace.py`:**\n  - `Unroll.__call__` passes a `SetEnvReference` through untouched.\n  - Inside a list, a reference is shape-checked and raises the \"set_env arrays require table references\u2026\" error when the shape is wrong.\n  - `_replace_ref` filters overrides by key and builds a `SetEnvReference` for `set_env` overrides.\n- **`set_env.py`:** `__iter__` now takes its list of exported-but-not-yet-read keys before it starts yielding. Without that, an export callback that reads another export dropped the second key from iteration.\n\nI didn't run anything beyond the `tests/config` command, and I didn't commit.", "ttft_ms": 3822, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 444782, "uuid": "a45f3643-ce36-482c-8db5-07de6e4a7baa", "ttft_stream_ms": 2830, "time_to_request_ms": 52, "first_content_frame_ms": 2830, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
